build-anywhere's additions to pnut's shell backend (the shell tier):

 - double and float, computed in software: literals are converted exactly
   when lexed (sh-float-lit.c), and a pass before code generation
   (sh-float.c) turns floating-point operations into calls to the
   soft-float library seed/pnut-libc/float.c; printf's %f, %e and %g go
   through ba_dfmt, and length modifiers such as %ld are dropped;
 - hooks in the runtime's getchar, read, write and close for terminals in
   non-canonical mode and for sockets (seed/pnut-libc/term.sh, net.sh).

Everything is under SH_SUPPORT_FLOAT and SH_BA_IO, which only the shell
target defines: pnut's x86 compiler (pnut-exe) is unchanged.

